::: {.fragment}
The results indicate a significant positive relationship between flipper length and body mass in Adelie penguins (β = 33, R^2^ = 0.22, p < 0.001) indicating that for every 1 mm increase in flipper length, the body mass is expected to increase by 33 grams. Based on the R^2^ value he model explains approximately 22% of the variance in body mass.
